  {
    "episode_id": 86471,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86471.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Well, it is going to be challenging. It's funny all my academic career, I was a professor. Now in the legislature, suddenly I'm the dean of the delegation. It's making me feel a little old and seasoned. But it's very exciting to have two new Democratic members from Nevada. We were certainly the bright spot on election night. And so now we have a delegation that's stronger in number, even though we have lost the leadership of Senator Reid, I suspect he'll stay involved. Recently, we got Gold Butte designated by the president. We're going to have to protect that and get the resources to be sure that it moves forward. We are going to have to fight Yucka Mountain. We know that that's an issue that they're going to bring back, now that Senator Reid has gone. And just immigration is a big issue for Nevada that will be a battle. So I think we are going to have our hands full and we're going to have to work as a unit that's going to be more important than ever.",
